    "result": "Excellent! All 28 tests now pass. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n**1. governance.test.js line 152 - Missing named export**\n- **Problem**: The test tried to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./finetune/index.js`, but it wasn't being exported\n- **Fix**: Added named exports for the schema constants (`APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`, `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`) to maintain backward compatibility while enabling the import\n\n**2. eval/index.test.js line 48 - Incorrect toxicity scoring**\n- **Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function signature expects `(outputs, bannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` was passing `(outputs, references)`. The references array was being treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging all outputs as toxic\n- **Fix**: Wrapped `toxicityMetric` in DEFAULT_METRICS with an object that has an `evaluate` method, ensuring it only receives the outputs parameter and uses the default banned terms\n\nBoth fixes maintain full backward compatibility:\n- All existing public exports remain available (both named and default)\n- No test files were modified\n- All 28 tests across 8 test files now pass \u2713",
